      <marc:subfield code="a">Ying Zi&apos;s rough brushstrokes, strong colors with a no-holds-barred emotional expression, and irregular compositions easily catch the reader&apos;s eye. 
 
Her painting style may seem reckless, but it contains themes of order in chaos, of nostalgic things, of nostalgic characters, of embracing the everyday, which is fascinating and captivating. 
 
Paired with a concise and to-the-point narration, it is not only interesting to see the artist&apos;s life, but also to remember the various similar people and things that have been around her. While flipping through Ying Zi&apos;s stories, one is able to savor small moments in one&apos;s own life that have been sealed away for years.</marc:subfield>
